2) VISUALIZATION STACK DECISION
--------------------------------------------------
Chosen stack (recommended)
- Primary chart engine: Apache ECharts
- React wrapper: echarts-for-react

Why this stack fits best
- Native support for radar + heatmap + advanced overlays needed by V3.
- High interactivity and flexible rendering (Canvas/SVG).
- Scales better for diagnostics and large trend datasets.
- Strong ecosystem and active maintenance.

Alternatives considered
- Recharts: excellent for simple dashboard charts, weaker for advanced heatmap/diagnostic use-cases.
- Chart.js: strong baseline charts, less natural for complex tutor-style composite visuals.
- visx: maximum control, but higher engineering cost and slower delivery.

Architecture policy (important)
- Keep current custom SVG in Practice Studio for domain-specific overlays.
- Use ECharts for analytics-first pages (radar/progress/diagnostics).
- Do not rewrite all existing V2 visuals at once.

